  "generated_text": "First, we need to substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the function \\( f(x) = 8x^3 - 6x^2 - 4x + 5 \\).\n\n\\[\nf(-2) = 8(-2)^3 - 6(-2)^2 - 4(-2) + 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate each term separately:\n\n\\[\n(-2)^3 = -8 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 8(-8) = -64\n\\]\n\\[\n(-2)^2 = 4 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad -6(4) = -24\n\\]\n\\[\n-4(-2) = 8\n\\]\n\nNow, add these results together:\n\n\\[\n-64 - 24 + 8 + 5\n\\]\n\nCombine the terms step by step:\n\n\\[\n-64 - 24 = -88\n\\]\n\\[\n-88 + 8 = -80\n\\]\n\\[\n-80 + 5 = -75\n\\]\n\nSo, \\( f(-2) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-75} \\).",
